# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
scripts/*.tmp

# Node / viewer
node_modules/
viewer/dist/
*.log

# Retrieved source material that is too large or not redistributable.
# SOURCE-REGISTER.md records the URL or the stock item for every one of these.
sources/dot_bridgereport15.pdf
sources/*.html
sources/videos/*
!sources/videos/.gitkeep
# Image BYTES are never stored. Metadata is: the photo-survey corpus is a list of URLs,
# licences and attributions with no third-party pixels in it, and the review sheet
# hotlinks rather than copies. So block the bytes precisely rather than the folder.
sources/photos/*.jpg
sources/photos/*.jpeg
sources/photos/*.png
sources/photos/*.tif
sources/photos/*.tiff

# Tavily search results. Leads, not sources - registration happens by hand in SOURCE-REGISTER.md.
data/leads/

# Never track anything that looks like a collapsed Windows path. curl strips the
# backslashes in a -K config's output value, which turns C:\Users\...\file.jpg into a
# single filename written into the current directory - i.e. straight into this repo.
# HOW-TO-DESIGN.md section 11 records the same accident with a relative curl -o loop.
Users*AppData*
C[A-Z]Users*

# Generated model artifacts are intentionally COMMITTED, not ignored:
#   mesh/glb/*, viewer/public/*.glb, viewer/public/parts.json,
#   viewer/metadata/*.json, tests/validation_report.json
# They are reproducible with `python scripts/build_control_skeleton.py`, but are tracked so the
# viewer runs from a clean clone and so changes to geometry show up in review diffs.

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
